WEBVTT

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.130
All right! Next!

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:39.840
Uchiyama!

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.800
Y-Yeah!

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.590
Here it comes!

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.800
What are you doing!?

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.430
Do you think you can beat Kaido like that!?

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:54.270
One more time!

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.000
Come on, what's wrong!?

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.740
Tashiro-senpai is stricter than usual today.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.690
Do it again!

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.730
I want to leave.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.700
Make sure you catch it!

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:13.870
Are you okay, Uchiyama?

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.450
He's fine!

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.880
Next: Fuji!

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.900
Just wait a second, Tashiro!

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.480
Why are you getting so irritated?

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:27.130
What'll we do if you injure someone with all these hard grounders!?

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:31.480
Don't you realize that we barely have enough members as it is!?

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.650
Yeah, that's true.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.220
Then put on some protection.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.400
There's no point in using that now!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.940
What do you mean, can't beat Kaido?

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:48.740
With these grounders, of course we won't beat Kaido!

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:55.550
Hey, stop that!

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.120
What are you arguing about?

00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.790
I'm leaving!

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:03.890
Practicing when I'm tired will just have the opposite effect!

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.630
What did we do to get so tired?

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.020
When we were up against Kawa Jitsu and Kuriyama,

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.600
what have we been able to do?

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.310
We've only made a few cuts here and there for Shigeno.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.980
T-That can't be helped!

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:25.770
Since the opponent's level has gotten so high, and we can't hit what we can't hit...

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.980
We can't do what we're incapable of!

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.160
That's why...

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.370
I'm saying we should do what we can.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:37.150
We might not have what it takes to beat Kaido.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.530
And maybe we're useless in the end, but...

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.890
I... want to help Shigeno, even just a little!

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:44.210
I... want to help Shigeno, even just a little!

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.710
That's what being a team is, right?

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.960
Fine.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:09.870
Good work.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:11.430
Here!

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.300
What's this for?

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.220
What's it for?

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:19.630
Looking over the players' conditions is the manager's job, after all.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:23.370
You were actually just making sure I wasn't skipping out, weren't you?

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.600
Isn't just running a bit boring?

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.530
There's no helping it... since I have this.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:30.930
There's no helping it... since I have this.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.600
I wonder if we can win... against Kaido.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:37.800
I wonder if we can win... against Kaido.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:38.930
Who knows?

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.350
<i>Because we have no way of practicing against a 150km/h fastball,</i>

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.780
<i>if we can get some practice with him,</i>

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.040
<i>it'll be a useful exercise before Koshien.</i>

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:56.160
Let's beat Kaido for sure!

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:02.830
We have to let Sato-senpai know that Seishuu's baseball club isn't just for practice!

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.680
Let's do this! Yeah!

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.750
P-Please wait a moment!

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:13.430
Are you saying I can't practice before the game against Kaido!?

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:14.980
There's no choice.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.810
Your foot won't be able to bear training, that's all.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.910
I can't do that!

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:24.180
They aren't opponents I can just relax against and expect to win!

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.890
Please, Doctor!

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.860
Isn't there anything you can do?

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.070
There's only one way I can recommend.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:47.220
This is great!

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:53.550
That doctor... Why didn't he tell me about this method earlier!?

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.900
<i>I don't feel any strain down here.</i>

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:05.150
<i>This way there won't be any extra pressure on my legs, and I can still work out!</i>

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.530
<i>It's two birds with one stone!</i>

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.960
Sorry, old lady!

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.430
All the young girls distracted me and I missed what was in front of me.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:22.150
Huh?

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:27.870
So why am I an old lady?

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:34.750
Well, somehow I felt like I bumped into something really big... so I thought...

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.390
MURDER CHOP!

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.830
So you and Shigeno-kun are childhood friends?

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:47.430
I'm so jealous!

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:48.190
Eh?

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:50.450
It's not just "eh."

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:56.520
He's been popular with the girls because of his latest activity in the prefectural tournament.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.880
R-Really?

00:06:58.880 --> 00:06:59.700
Him?

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.310
I mean, doesn't he look pretty cool?

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.370
If you're childhood friends, you should go out with him.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:14.000
Well, if he's not your type, that's another story.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.210
I thought you two fit well together back there.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.930
He's not <i>that</i> type.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:24.640
He's not the type to go out with girls.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:31.490
Just like the old days, only baseball and his sweaty rivals are reflected in his eyes.

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:36.710
But I think I'm fine with that.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:41.120
<i>I'm still fine with that.</i>

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:46.790
You're the late-bloomer type.

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:47.540
Huh?

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:57.760
Yeah, ice cream after going to the pool is the best!

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:58.460
Nice and cold!

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:01.640
It's in five days, right?

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:02.690
The game against Kaido.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:03.470
Yeah.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:07.190
According to Taiga, it seems like another person's injured.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:10.850
Are you okay like that?

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.280
To heck if I know.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:16.530
Well, with your younger brother, it'll be fine.

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:18.830
I'm asking about your injury!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:23.580
Want a bite?

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.030
No thanks.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:30.130
I know your ambition is the game against Kaido, but...

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:32.080
don't push yourself too hard.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:36.290
They aren't...

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.420
They aren't opponents we can defeat without pushing ourselves.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.100
Honda!

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:54.910
Don't worry!

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:57.780
The heavens are completely on my side right now!

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:11.740
That idiot.

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.630
Don't depend on something like this for luck.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.500
It'll take a full month to heal!?

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.180
S-Sorry!

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:26.640
B-But it's just my left hand, so I can catch pop flies somehow...

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:29.880
Just taking pop flies... That won't...

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.630
What about batting!?

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.600
You can't even hold the bat like that!

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.730
Sorry...

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.780
How about you, Shimizu-kun?

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:44.110
At least, compared to Yamamoto-senpai, I can hold the bat.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:50.280
Although I'm worried about having to throw the ball like I did in the previous game.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:53.870
What kind of a game will we have against Kaido like this?

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:19.980
Everyone, good work.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:24.320
For now, I believe we've done what we could.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.910
Tomorrow is finally the game against Kaido.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.780
Let's play a game without any regrets.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:34.490
Yes, sir!

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:36.320
So it's finally coming up tomorrow.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.580
I'm getting nervous.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:39.200
I might not get any sleep tonight!

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:47.270
Today might've been the last time we practice here.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.400
We all made this place.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:55.030
Who knew that we would've been playing baseball back then?

00:10:58.500 --> 00:10:59.420
Sorry.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:03.470
Even though the result of tomorrow's game hasn't been decided yet,

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:04.900
I'm saying weird things.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:14.530
Let's get going.

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:16.730
Miyazaki.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.010
Make sure you bring a spare pair of glasses!

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:20.930
It'll be trouble if you break them again.

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:22.990
Yeah, I have them.

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:30.850
Hey, Fuji!

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.570
If you don't hurry up, I'll lock the classroom door!

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:43.540
What are you doing?

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:47.760
We've already done ground maintenance.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:48.880
Yeah.

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:52.280
Well, I just felt like doing this.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:10.060
Nakamura.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:12.800
I... haven't apologized to you about that time yet, have I?

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:16.760
I... haven't apologized to you about that time yet, have I?

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:27.910
What's this all of a sudden?

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:29.450
I... was really scared at that time,

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:32.120
I... was really scared at that time,

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:38.040
and I... ran away without... saying anything.

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:47.040
Because of the injury, you were out of school for a whole month and had to graduate like that.

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:48.940
That...

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:51.860
It wasn't a month.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.730
It was two months!

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.090
That's why I couldn't go to the graduation ceremony.

00:12:57.090 --> 00:13:01.490
Plus I was late for the athletics entrance exam for the middle school I wanted to get into.

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:04.800
S-Sorry.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:05.900
S-Sorry.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:14.030
Even if you apologize at this point,

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:16.540
it won't make up for those memories I'll never have.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:18.900
But...

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.540
in place of that,

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:25.550
if you defeat Kaido and bring us to Koshien,

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:28.000
I might let the sea carry it away.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:41.140
This is a free fansub.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:41.140
Not for sale or rent.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:44.850
So it's at the Oceans Stadium today, eh?

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:45.920
Yeah.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.120
The traffic is clear today too.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:51.370
We should go and cheer you on.

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:52.190
You don't have to.

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:54.430
The weather doesn't look good today,

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:58.950
and it's not like today is going to be our last game.

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:01.380
If you want to come, wait until Koshien.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.120
All right.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:07.160
Then, I'm going!

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:09.130
Do your best!

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:11.090
What's this!?

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:13.530
Katsudon in the morning? {the katsu in katsudon can also mean "to win," so she's serving it to him as a good luck wish}

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:15.060
What are you saying?

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.180
You're up against Kaido!

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:20.620
You don't have a chance if you don't have a good omen or something with you!

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:27.180
It's finally here.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:31.150
Well, I won't just say good luck to you.

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:34.660
Come back to us safe.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:37.110
Yeah.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.870
I'm off!

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:48.160
I'll head to work.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:50.370
Do you want to go to the game?

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:54.280
I won't.

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:58.990
I don't think I'll be able to watch.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:18.670
Huh?

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:20.530
Shimizu-san?

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:22.130
Komori!

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:33.500
T-This is the Oceans Stadium?

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:34.880
The fence is so high!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:38.550
<i>Dad...</i>

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:42.250
<i>I'm back here again.</i>

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:47.020
Seishuu Private, please start your warmup.

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:49.220
All right!

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:02.800
They're here... Kaido!

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:04.180
They're here... Kaido! 

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:16.730
Sato-senpai is amazing, as expected.

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:18.040
Really?

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:21.550
It's warmup, so that's just a given.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:45.880
<i>I want to be a player like that too.</i>

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:50.620
That's what I thought when I started baseball.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.830
It doesn't matter to little kids.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:55.850
L-Little kids?

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:57.340
Aren't we in the same grade!?

00:16:57.340 --> 00:16:59.330
Seishuu, bow!

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.800
All right!

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:09.650
Play!

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:11.850
Let's have a good game!

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:14.150
Hey, Miyake!

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:15.900
Kokubu, Kodama!

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:21.660
So you guys stayed on the first team.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:26.740
Yeah. Unfortunately, it's taking all we can just to stay on the bench.

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:28.950
Looks like you're doing well too, Shigeno.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:31.490
Hey, they'll yell at us.

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:39.380
Fielding for Kaido Academy High School...

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:42.340
Pitcher: Ichihara-kun.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:45.050
Catcher: Sato-kun.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:47.520
First baseman: Ohba-kun.

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:49.730
Second baseman: Tokashiki-kun.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.970
Third baseman: Yakushiji-kun.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.680
Shortstop: Izumi-kun.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.440
Left fielder: Ishimatsu-kun.

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:01.190
Center fielder: Kusano-kun.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.910
Right fielder: Yaoita-kun.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:11.090
Ichihara's the pitcher?

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:13.210
It's not the ace, Mayumura?

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:16.840
Kaido has a pitching rotation.

00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:19.880
They won't bring out Mayumura first since he played in the last game...

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:21.890
Didn't we say that at the meeting!?

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:25.720
Well, whoever it is, we won't be able to hit it anyway.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:28.970
So what?

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:32.440
We'll just force them to bring him out.

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.280
It's finally here.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:35.890
Yeah.

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:40.850
I didn't actually think he would come here under the circumstances.

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:45.950
Although the chances of defeating Kaido right now are impossible.

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:51.210
At least it'd be nice if they made a good game of it.

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:56.960
Top of the first inning: leading off for Seishuu High School...

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:01.580
Batting first: right fielder, Shimizu-kun.

00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:10.520
Play ball!

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:16.890
Strike!

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:20.530
H-Hey, that's fast!

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:21.850
It's not just that.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:24.720
He has complete control over his pitches and speed.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.280
After Mayumura, he's a rising candidate to be drafted.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:30.610
Strike!

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:31.840
Hey, hey.

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:34.290
Who's going to force him to switch out?

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:38.290
Fuji, quit it with your babbling.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:41.240
He hasn't even struck anyone out,

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.750
yet you don't think you can get a hit against him?

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:51.770
He hit it!

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:53.220
Nice, Taiga!

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:54.460
All right!

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.680
Good going, Taiga!

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:58.400
Just as expected from my kouhai!

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:02.110
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:03.450
Hit it!

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:04.500
Keep it going!

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:07.280
Get a headstart and surprise them!

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:09.230
We aren't afraid of Kaido at all!

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:19.500
First!

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:22.630
Out!

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:24.970
A successful sacrifice bunt!

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:26.170
Nice, Uchiyama!

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:31.030
Batting third: pitcher, Shigeno-kun.

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.140
They might walk him.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:42.130
They might not do it right from the start like we did,

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:46.150
but Kaido knows Honda-kun's abilities for sure.

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:49.430
He's the most dangerous batter for Seishuu.

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:55.290
With first base open, I can't imagine Toshiya-kun giving him a real challenge.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.290
Ball!

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:00.030
Ball!

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:02.380
Looks like they're walking him.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:08.530
You let the weaker batter hit for your own profit,

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:12.710
but you'll really just walk the strong batter?

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:14.480
Strong batter?

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:15.720
You?

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:20.810
Fine.

00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:25.430
If you say it like that, I'll just have to send the ball flying!

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:28.020
Ball!

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:29.500
Ball three!

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:32.370
Damn, they're really going to walk Shigeno.

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:34.510
I won't hit it!

00:21:34.510 --> 00:21:37.330
I won't be fooled by those pitches.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:41.030
I still need to let our fourth batter, Tashiro, up here.

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:43.170
You're talkative.

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:48.490
Let me just say this: Kaido's manual doesn't say to walk someone...

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:51.130
in fear of allowing a run or two at the beginning of the game.

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:55.420
Strike!

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:57.730
A-A challenge?

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:01.690
<i>Well, thanks for that!</i>

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:04.690
Foul!

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:17.120
I thought I was being underestimated for a while there.

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:19.580
Well, it's fine if you underestimate me.

00:22:19.580 --> 00:22:25.910
I'll let you know what you're risking with that carefree attitude!

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:32.460
Strike!

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:34.470
Batter out!

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:35.650
<i>A-A forkball?</i>

00:22:35.650 --> 00:22:36.970
<i>A-A forkball?</i>

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:39.120
<i>That Ichihara... </i>

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:41.690
<i>He wasn't able to throw a forkball before!</i>

00:22:41.690 --> 00:22:45.740
Everyone rose another level in the past year.

00:22:46.560 --> 00:22:49.080
We're not underestimating you, Goro-kun,

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:50.850
nor do we think little of you.

00:22:51.330 --> 00:22:53.850
But, we have confidence.

00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:59.530
We have the absolute confidence that our development over the year won't lose to yours.

00:23:00.110 --> 00:23:05.680
In fact, Goro-kun, aren't you the one thinking little of us?

00:24:41.660 --> 00:24:46.250
Kaido's strict baseball manual is slowly driving Seishuu into a corner.

00:24:46.250 --> 00:24:48.730
At this rate, the pace will fall right out of our hands!

00:24:48.730 --> 00:24:50.730
We have to overcome it somehow!

00:24:52.650 --> 00:24:53.650
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.650 --> 00:24:55.930
No Openings! The Baseball Manual.

00:24:55.930 --> 00:24:58.350
Run to the stage of your dreams!
